yle="stroke:none" d="M 6.09 0 L -3.65 4.87 L 0 0 L -3.65 -4.87"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF4D4D;--ltx-fill-color:#FF4D4D;--ltx-fg-color:#FF4D4D;" color="#FF4D4D" fill="#FF4D4D" stroke="#FF4D4D" stroke-width="2.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 53.75 4.59 L 102.4 -53.78"></path><g transform="matrix(0.64027 -0.76814 0.76814 0.64027 102.4 -53.78)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 6.09 0 L -3.65 4.87 L 0 0 L -3.65 -4.87"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4DFF;" color="#4D4DFF" fill="#4D4DFF" stroke="#4D4DFF" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -18.6 -96.69 C 92.7 -145.82 185.63 -112.09 267.59 4.99"></path><g transform="matrix(0.57347 0.81923 -0.81923 0.57347 267.59 4.99)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4DFF;" color="#4D4DFF" fill="#4D4DFF" stroke="#4D4DFF" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 155.91 -58.46 L 252.51 5.94"></path><g transform="matrix(0.83209 0.55464 -0.55464 0.83209 252.51 5.94)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fill-color:#4D4DFF;--ltx-fg-color:#4D4DFF;" color="#4D4DFF" fill="#4D4DFF" stroke="#4D4DFF" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 283.46 45.22 L 283.46 110.64"></path><g transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 283.46 110.64)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 3.6 0 L -2.16 2.88 L 0 0 L -2.16 -2.88"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fill-color:#3333FF;--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;" color="#3333FF" fill="#3333FF" stroke="#3333FF" transform="matrix(0.85 0.0 0.0 0.85 -360.06 421.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:5.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:13.5pt;" color="#000000" height="14.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.39)" width="97.9"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#3333FF;">Input Layer</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#33FF33;--ltx-fill-color:#33FF33;--ltx-fg-color:#33FF33;" color="#33FF33" fill="#33FF33" stroke="#33FF33" transform="matrix(0.85 0.0 0.0 0.85 -373.12 315.37)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:6.86em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:13.5pt;" color="#000000" height="14.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.53)" width="128.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#33FF33;">Encoding Layer</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF9933;--ltx-fill-color:#FF9933;--ltx-fg-color:#FF9933;" color="#FF9933" fill="#FF9933" stroke="#FF9933" transform="matrix(0.85 0.0 0.0 0.85 -374.22 219.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:7.08em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:13.5pt;" color="#000000" height="14.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.53)" width="132.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF9933;">Attention Layer</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#CC3366;--ltx-fill-color:#CC3366;--ltx-fg-color:#CC3366;" color="#CC3366" fill="#CC3366" stroke="#CC3366" transform="matrix(0.85 0.0 0.0 0.85 -377.64 129.34)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:7.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:13.5pt;" color="#000000" height="14.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.53)" width="138.74"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#CC3366;">Processing Layer</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF3333;--ltx-fill-color:#FF3333;--ltx-fg-color:#FF3333;" color="#FF3333" fill="#FF3333" stroke="#FF3333" transform="matrix(0.85 0.0 0.0 0.85 -379.46 23.05)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:7.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:13.5pt;" color="#000000" height="14.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.53)" width="143.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF3333;">Generation Layer</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#339999;--ltx-fill-color:#339999;--ltx-fg-color:#339999;" color="#339999" fill="#339999" stroke="#339999" transform="matrix(0.85 0.0 0.0 0.85 -366.15 -83.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-fo-width:6.01em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:13.5pt;" color="#000000" height="14.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.39)" width="112.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F1.pic1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:120%;--ltx-fg-color:#339999;">Output Layer</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>Enhanced GenRec Framework Architecture: A comprehensive system integrating five key innovations - ① Multimodal Fusion with cross-modal attention, ② Retrieval-Augmented Generation, ③ Causal Inference-based Debiasing, ④ Explainable Recommendation Generation, and ⑤ Real-time Adaptive Learning. The framework processes heterogeneous inputs through specialized encoders and generates personalized recommendations with natural language explanations.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Multimodal Fusion Architecture</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our multimodal fusion architecture addresses the challenge of integrating heterogeneous data sources commonly available in recommendation datasets through a hierarchical attention mechanism. The architecture consists of three primary components: modality-specific encoders, cross-modal attention layers, and fusion aggregation modules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modality-Specific Encoders:</span> For each modality <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{text,categorical,numerical\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{text,categorical,numerical\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we employ specialized encoders to extract feature representations:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{m}^{(i)}=f_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{m}^{(i)};\theta_{m})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{m}^{(i)}=f_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{m}^{(i)};\theta_{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{m}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{m}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the raw input for modality <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and item <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the modality-specific encoder function, and <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are the learnable parameters. For textual content, we use transformer encoders:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{text}^{(i)}=\text{Transformer}(\mathbf{E}\cdot\mathbf{w}^{(i)}+\mathbf{P})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Transformer</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{text}^{(i)}=\text{Transformer}(\mathbf{E}\cdot\mathbf{w}^{(i)}+\mathbf{P})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the embedding matrix, <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> are token indices, and <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math> are positional encodings.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-Modal Attention:</span> We implement asymmetric cross-modal attention to capture inter-modal relationships:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{m\rightarrow n}=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{m}\mathbf{K}_{n}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{m\rightarrow n}=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{m}\mathbf{K}_{n}^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{m\leftarrow n}^{(i)}=\mathbf{A}_{m\rightarrow n}\mathbf{V}_{n}\mathbf{h}_{n}^{(i)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{m\leftarrow n}^{(i)}=\mathbf{A}_{m\rightarrow n}\mathbf{V}_{n}\mathbf{h}_{n}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are query, key, and value matrices for modalities <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fusion Aggregation:</span> The final multimodal representation is computed through adaptive weighted fusion:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{fused}^{(i)}=\sum_{m}\alpha_{m}\cdot\mathbf{h}_{m}^{(i)}+\beta\cdot\text{MLP}([\mathbf{h}_{text}^{(i)};\mathbf{h}_{visual}^{(i)};\mathbf{h}_{audio}^{(i)}])" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>MLP</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{fused}^{(i)}=\sum_{m}\alpha_{m}\cdot\mathbf{h}_{m}^{(i)}+\beta\cdot\text{MLP}([\mathbf{h}_{text}^{(i)};\mathbf{h}_{visual}^{(i)};\mathbf{h}_{audio}^{(i)}])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are learned attention weights computed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{m}=\frac{\exp(\mathbf{w}_{m}^{T}\mathbf{h}_{m}^{(i)})}{\sum_{n}\exp(\mathbf{w}_{n}^{T}\mathbf{h}_{n}^{(i)})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{m}=\frac{\exp(\mathbf{w}_{m}^{T}\mathbf{h}_{m}^{(i)})}{\sum_{n}\exp(\mathbf{w}_{n}^{T}\mathbf{h}_{n}^{(i)})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ III-B Multimodal Fusion Architecture ‣ III Methodology ‣ LLM4Rec: Large Language Models for Multimodal Generative Recommendation with Causal Debiasing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> illustrates the detailed architecture of our multimodal fusion mechanism, showing how different modalities are processed and integrated through cross-modal attention.</p>
</div>
